The projects below contain no code in this distribution and impose no license
obligation on it. They are recorded because their published design influenced
this work, and because two pieces of terminology were adopted verbatim.

CodeGraph -- https://github.com/ColbyMchenry/codegraph
    MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Colby Mchenry

    Adopted as ideas and naming, not as code:
      - "sufficient-or-silent" as the contract for any advisory output: give a
        complete answer or stay quiet, never a partial one.
      - `name_segment_vocab` as the name of the prose-to-identifier mapping in
        the generated search index. The implementation here is our own.
      - success-shaped errors: an expected condition returns guidance and a
        zero exit status, reserving nonzero for genuine malfunction.
      - staleness honesty: serve results with a "computed at <commit>" banner
        rather than blocking or silently serving stale data.

Spec Kit -- https://github.com/github/spec-kit
    MIT, Copyright GitHub, Inc.

    Adopted as ideas only, with no code and no shared naming:
      - a declarative integration registry, so adding an agent is data rather
        than new code.
      - neutral command tokens in canonical sources, resolved per adapter.
      - hash-tracked install manifests, so regeneration and uninstall touch
        only files whose contents still match what was generated.
